  segment) is the major target of injury in ARF, others have held the view that damage to the distal nephron            
  [particularly the medullary thick ascending limb (MTAL) segment] plays a more important role in this disease. In      
  this discussion, the first of three on different aspects of ARF that have been hotly debated, we have invited         
